# Owned seed SQL is embedded byte-for-byte (base64) in module definitions and
# validated with a strict byte-for-byte + sha256 check by
# scripts/omp/validate-component-versions.ps1. Pin LF so git checkouts are
# deterministic on every platform regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sql text eol=lf

# docs-agent/ is generated output that scripts/verify-agent-docs-fresh.mjs
# compares byte-for-byte against HEAD. The comparison is raw: it bypasses
# clean filters and the stat cache, so any CRLF a Windows checkout writes
# would turn the gate red on an otherwise fresh tree even when no generator
# was rerun. Pin LF so git itself writes LF on every platform regardless of
# core.autocrlf, which makes the comparison regeneration-independent and
# closes the "opposite verdicts for the same HEAD" failure class the gate
# exists to remove. All 30 HEAD blobs are already LF; renormalization is a
# no-op (proved in the commit that introduced this line).
docs-agent/** text eol=lf

# scripts/omp/*.ps1 are verbatim copies of OpenModulePlatform's shared scripts,
# compared byte-for-byte by Check 15 (validate-shared-scripts.ps1) against the
# platform checkout, which pins "*.ps1 text eol=crlf". Mirror that rule so the
# working-tree bytes match the platform (CRLF) while the blobs stay LF, which
# also keeps the pre-commit whitespace check (git diff --check) green.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
